.TH RECEIVE 2N UniSoft
.SH NAME
receive \- receive message from a socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <net/socket.h>
.sp
.B cc = receive(s, from, buf, len);
.br
.B int cc, s;
.br
.B struct sockaddr *from;
.br
.B char *buf;
.br
.B int len;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Receive\^
is used to receive a message from a 
.SM SOCK_DGRAM
or 
.SM SOCK_RAW 
socket.
The source address of the message is placed in
.IR from .
The length of the message is returned in
.IR cc .
If the message is too long to fit in the supplied buffer,
then excess characters are discarded.
.PP
If no messages are available at the socket, the
.I receive\^
waits for a message to arrive, unless the socket is nonblocking
in which case a
.I cc\^
of \-1 is returned with the external variable errno set to 
.SM EWOULDBLOCK\*S.
.PP
The
.IR select\^ (2N)
call may be used to determine when more data arrives.
.SH SEE ALSO
send(2), socket(2N).
.SH BUGS
.PP
This call is provisional and will exist in a slightly different form
in future releases.
.\"N	 @(#)receive.2N	 5.2 of 7/12/84
